# GoldenEye: Rogue Agent (4541005D), SAVE. The first-run route up to player
# control, then `flush`, so the PLAYER1 profile it creates reaches the disk.
#
# Why a separate route: every first-run so far (nav session 09-26 19:25, its
# replay 19:32, titlebench 23:30, all on the Nova) ended in a force-stop with
# no flush, and the next boot showed CREATE NEW PROFILE again. This route
# exists to leave the save on the disk for titlestate.py to extract. It has
# no `mark gameplay`: the title is paused by the flush, so the run makes a
# save and is not a measurement.
#
# The steps are goldeneye-ra.first-run.route's, lines 22-121, unchanged.
wait 27.0
shot boot
wait 7.9
press A
wait 5.1
shot a1
wait 0.6
press START
wait 5.1
shot start1
wait 9.6
press START
wait 6.1
shot start2
wait 9.4
press START
wait 3.1
shot kb-start
wait 8.2
press LEFT
wait 1.6
shot kb-left
wait 11.3
axis LX max
wait 0.4
axis LX mid
wait 1.1
shot kb-lx
wait 11.5
axis LX max
wait 0.3
axis LX mid
wait 0.7
axis LX max
wait 0.4
axis LX mid
wait 0.7
axis LX max
wait 0.3
axis LX mid
wait 0.7
axis LX max
wait 0.4
axis LX mid
wait 0.7
axis LX max
wait 0.4
axis LX mid
wait 0.7
axis LX max
wait 0.3
axis LX mid
wait 0.8
axis LX max
wait 0.4
axis LX mid
wait 0.7
axis LX max
wait 0.4
axis LX mid
wait 0.7
axis LX max
wait 0.3
axis LX mid
wait 0.6
shot kb-ok
wait 9.7
press A
wait 5.1
shot ok
wait 8.5
mark profile-created
wait 0.8
press A
wait 5.1
shot campaign
wait 9.8
press A
wait 12.1
shot play
wait 22.3
shot load2
wait 0.6
press START
wait 5.1
shot skip
wait 9.3
press A
wait 4.1
shot skipA
wait 22.0
shot fmv3
wait 40.6
shot fmv4
wait 9.4
axis RX max
wait 1.2
axis RX mid
wait 0.6
shot look-right
wait 10
shot control
flush 20
wait 5
shot flushed
